# This CITATION.cff file describes how to cite this software.
# GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button once this file is present.
#
# TODO after the first Zenodo release:
#   - set `version` to the released version (e.g. "1.0")
#   - set `date-released` to that release's date (YYYY-MM-DD)
#   - uncomment and fill in `doi` with the DOI Zenodo mints for the release
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OxySim-129"
abstract: >-
  A high-fidelity OpenFOAM-based C++ framework for carbonaceous solid fuel
  combustion, covering scales from single-particle studies to MW-scale
  reactor simulations. Provides solvers and libraries for coal and biomass
  combustion coupled to flamelet-based tabulated chemistry.
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/STFS-TUDa/oxysim-129"
url: "https://github.com/STFS-TUDa/oxysim-129"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
authors:
